{"text": "6902\nBiochemical Special Investigations\nB.D. Davies\nSeptember, 1990\n\nI. ADDITIONAL APPROACHES TOWARD PUTRESCINE METHYLTRANSFERASE:\n(PMT) ISOLATION:\n\nA. Objective: Provide additional experimental approaches to assist in the effort to isolate PMT.\n\nB. Results: An aliquot of PS-PMT tail fraction was sent to Protein Technologies Inc for\nfractionation on their RF3 preparative isoelectric focusing instrument. Following IEF\nPurification, the fractions were retumed to PM and analyzed for enzyme activity, total protein\ncontent, and SDS-PAGE protein separation pattems. Examination of the results of those\nanalyses indicated that 60% of the starting enzyme activity was recovered._In addition, there was\nseparation between the samples containing the highest enzyme activity and those containing the\nhighest protein concentrations.\n\nC. Plans: Perform one additional fractionation using optimized determined from the first\nfractionation and make a determination as to whether or not to purchase the instrument.\n\nD. References: Davies, B. Notebook Number 8638, pp. 190-192.\n\n6zszspezoe",
